  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5103",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is linked to J-RT3-T3-5 through a series of molecular interactions involving purinoceptors and a common chemical compound. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin targets P2X purinoceptor 1, which is subsequently targeted by [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, a compound that also targets J-RT3-T3-5. Similarly, doxorubicin is associated with NCI-H46, which is also targeted by the same compound, reinforcing the connection between doxorubicin and J-RT3-T3-5. The presence of a shared target compound, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, suggests a potential mechanism of action where the compound may modulate purinoceptor activity, thereby influencing J-RT3-T3-5. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for this compound in mediating the effects of doxorubicin on J-RT3-T3-5, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
